@startuml activity-fr-01
' Report §2.1 — FR-01 Create a draft event.
' Source: EventController.createDraft, CreateEventRequest, EventApplicationService.createDraft,
' Event.createDraft, DateRange, GlobalExceptionHandler.
!include include/style.iuml
!include include/activity.iuml

title FR-01 — Create a draft event

|Organiser|
start
:POST /api/v1/events
{name, description,
 venue {name, addressLine, city},
 startDate, endDate};

|event-catalog-service|
:EventController.createDraft
validates CreateEventRequest (@Valid);
if (name blank, venue missing, a venue
field blank, or a date missing?) then (yes)
  $ERR:400 VALIDATION_FAILED;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:CreateEventRequest.toCommand()
builds Venue and DateRange value objects;
if (endDate before startDate?) then (yes)
  $ERR:400 INVALID_REQUEST
  "date range end must not precede its start";
  stop
else (no)
endif
:EventApplicationService.createDraft
Event.createDraft(new UUID, name, description,
venue, dateRange) → status DRAFT, no sessions;
:EventRepository.save
→ catalogdb.events;
$OK:201 Created
EventResponse (status "DRAFT", sessions []);

|Organiser|
:keeps the event id
for FR-02 and FR-03;
stop

note right
  A draft publishes no event:
  nothing outside the Programme
  context hears about it until
  sessions are added (FR-02).
end note
@enduml
